00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:23.900
JEN PERSON: Most
businesses depend

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.700
on a diverse array
of technologies

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.860
to operate day-to-day.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.470
Your clients need a way to
interface with products,

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.770
like viewing products
via a website or an app.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:37.200
Employees need to access company
services on their laptops,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.590
tablets, and phones.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.380
Companies need to manage
onboarding and off-boarding

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.780
employees in directories.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.300
And the business may depend
on third-party services,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.510
like customer management systems
and messaging applications.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.740
Some of these services
may exist on premises.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.690
But other services
are most useful

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.240
when they are accessible
outside of the office.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.220
Personally, I both
love and loathe

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.380
that I can check my
work email on my devices

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.280
from any location.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.880
So how can a business
effectively maintain

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.180
secure access to all
these technologies?

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.090
Well, one great solution to
this tangle of technologies

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.550
is Google Cloud Identity.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.550
Cloud Identity is a unified
solution for your business's

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.260
identity needs.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.830
It protects company data using
the BeyondCorp security model

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.350
and Google's threat
intelligence signals.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.960
And it enables people
to access thousands

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.230
of apps with single sign on and
manage their company accounts

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:37.340
using the same process as
their personal Google accounts.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.370
Cloud Identity helps your
company transition to the cloud

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.930
by integrating
with your existing

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.330
systems on a reliable,
trusted platform.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.480
So to boil it all
down, Cloud Identity

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.690
is a suite of products that help
your company unify management

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.420
of people, apps, and devices.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.730
Now if I went in
depth on everything

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.030
that Cloud Identity does, that
would be a very long video.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.160
So rather than try to
squeeze all this information

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.640
into a single video, I've
decided to make this series,

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.000
"Who's There, Exploring
Cloud Identity."

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.919
I'll be talking about
four main facets

00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:14.270
to Cloud Identity-- managing
users, devices, directories,

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.930
and apps.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.170
We'll explore each
facet of Cloud Identity

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:21.170
in depth, starting with
managing app authentication

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.878
and authorization through
Cloud Identity platform.

